  txnOnly: 'The model wrote only transaction commands (BEGIN/COMMIT) — no SQL to run.',
  orphanRetry: "AUTOMATIC CHECK: Real declared foreign-key constraints were violated and the entire batch was rolled back; no data changed. Bad links observed in the failed batch before rollback: {d}. Parent-key examples observed in that same failed-batch snapshot: {v}; this snapshot describes the failed attempt, not a new observation after rollback; the list is neither every key nor the maximum ID. Correct only the original user's requested scope. Reparenting, deletion, NULL links, new parent records or schema changes are allowed only when part of that original request. Give the complete corrected SQL in one sql block. If the request cannot satisfy the existing constraints while preserving the required links, explain the specific blocker clearly without SQL. Do not dismiss a declared relationship as coincidental name similarity.",
  orphanStillBad: "AI tried to fix it but orphan rows persist, SQL was not executed: {d}. Valid ids: {v}.",
  orphanFixed: "Orphan rows caught, AI fixed and executed.",
  childlessRetry: "AUTOMATIC CHECK: some parent rows you added in this run have no related rows — data was written but is incomplete. Missing rows and READY TEMPLATES: {d}. Do this: 1) Give the templates unchanged in a single ```sql block (only the complementary SQL, do not rewrite everything). Each template clones a valid row — do not change the column list or the SELECT. 2) If there is no template (child table is empty), write the missing rows with fresh INSERTs, putting the listed parent ids into the link column. 3) If this parent genuinely needs NO child — especially an event table whose status column does not call for it (like a refund for a non-refunded payment) — answer without SQL, the block is lifted.",
  childlessNote: "Note: these parents have no related rows: {d}.",
